# LeakSanitizer suppressions for PracticeTakesTests.
#
# A suppression is a decision to stop looking at something. Every entry below
# therefore names what it silences and why this repository cannot fix it, so
# that the decision is reviewable rather than inherited.
#
# Nothing here may suppress a leak originating in src/. If a report names a
# frame in this project's own code, the fix is the code, not this file.
#
# Applied automatically to `ctest` runs of a build tree configured with
# -DPRACTICE_TAKES_SANITIZE=address. Running the test binary directly needs it
# passed by hand:
#
#   LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tools/sanitizers/lsan.supp ./build-asan/PracticeTakesTests

# fontconfig, reached through JUCE's font enumeration the first time anything
# measures or draws text. It caches pattern, charset, and value objects for the
# lifetime of the process and releases them only from FcFini(), which JUCE does
# not call — deliberately, since the cache is shared and tearing it down mid-run
# would be worse than leaking it. Roughly 8.8 kB in 128 allocations on a
# headless Linux runner.
#
# Reported against libfontconfig 2.15 via FcValueSave and FcConfigCreate.
leak:libfontconfig
